WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.000
When dealing with a bite from an animal or even another person, your two main concerns are managing the bleeding and preventing infection.

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:18.000
It is also important to remember that certain mammals, like raccoons, skunks, and bats, can transmit rabies through a bite, which is a very serious medical situation.

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:21.000
If someone is bitten, follow these steps to provide care.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:26.000
First, ensure the scene is safe so you don't become the next victim.

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:31.000
Second, wash the wound gently with soap and water to help prevent infection.

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:36.000
Third, control any bleeding by applying firm, direct pressure.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:40.000
You can also apply an ice pack to the area to help reduce pain and swelling.

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:46.000
If the bite breaks the skin at all, the person needs to contact a health care provider for further treatment.

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:57.000
However, you should call 911 immediately if there is severe bleeding that won't stop, if the person is still in danger, or if you have any reason to suspect the animal might have rabies.

